From: Roy Klopper <roy.klopper@stealthscale.io>
Subject: [PATCH] bash-engine: never drop a marker line over a quote in the trace

The bash engine tracks single quotes across trace lines, so that the
rest of a '...' word that spans lines is not printed as output. While
it believes a quote is open it drops every line, marker lines included.
Two kinds of trace line leave it in that state by mistake:

- xtrace prints the words of a [[ ]] test as they are. A value with a
  quote in it, [[ -z it's ]], has one quote on the line.
- bash 5.3 prints words with control characters as $'...' and escapes
  a quote inside as \'. The engine counts that quote.

After either, the engine reports nothing until another line happens to
have an odd number of quotes. bats-core 1.14 saves the traps in `run`
with such a $'...' word, so on bash 5.3 a bats suite reports no
coverage at all.

A marker starts a command, so no quote is open in front of it: reset
the state on every marker line and attribute the line. Keep the state
for lines without a marker, which is what hides the rest of a quoted
word. Read $'...' with its escapes.
---
 src/engines/bash-engine.cc |   25 ++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/engines/bash-engine.cc b/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
--- a/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
+++ b/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 	INPUT_NORMAL,       // No multiline stuff
 	INPUT_QUOTE,        // "
 	INPUT_SINGLE_QUOTE, // '
+	INPUT_ANSI_QUOTE,   // $'...', backslash escapes inside, never spans lines
 	INPUT_MULTILINE,    // backslash backslash
 };
 
@@ -280,17 +281,20 @@
 		std::string cur(curLine);
 		// Line markers always start with kcov@
 
-		if (m_inputType == INPUT_SINGLE_QUOTE) {
-			m_inputType = getInputType(cur);
-			return true;
-		}
-
 		size_t kcovStr = cur.find("kcov@");
 		if (kcovStr == std::string::npos)
 		{
-			fprintf(stderr, "%s", cur.c_str());
+			// The rest of a single-quoted word that spans lines is not
+			// output. Any other line without a marker is.
+			if (m_inputType != INPUT_SINGLE_QUOTE)
+				fprintf(stderr, "%s", cur.c_str());
+			m_inputType = getInputType(cur);
 			return true;
 		}
+		// A marker starts a command, so no quote is open in front of it. A
+		// quote in the data of a [[ ]] test, which xtrace prints as is, must
+		// not hide the commands after it.
+		m_inputType = INPUT_NORMAL;
 		m_inputType = getInputType(cur);
 
 		std::vector<std::string> parts = split_string(cur.substr(kcovStr), "@");
@@ -534,13 +538,20 @@
 		return out;
 	}
 
+	// Follows the quoting of bash's xtrace output: '...' may span lines, and $'...'
+	// (bash 5.3 uses it for words with control characters) escapes with backslashes,
+	// \' included, so a quote inside it does not end it.
 	enum InputType getInputType(const std::string &str)
 	{
 		enum InputType out = m_inputType;
 
 		for(std::string::size_type i = 0; i < str.size(); ++i) {
-			if (str[i] == '\\' && out == INPUT_NORMAL)
+			if (str[i] == '\\' && out != INPUT_SINGLE_QUOTE)
 				i++;
+			else if (str[i] == '\'' && out == INPUT_ANSI_QUOTE)
+				out = INPUT_NORMAL;
+			else if (str[i] == '\'' && out == INPUT_NORMAL && i > 0 && str[i - 1] == '$')
+				out = INPUT_ANSI_QUOTE;
 			else if (str[i] == '\'')
 				out = (out == INPUT_NORMAL ? INPUT_SINGLE_QUOTE : INPUT_NORMAL);
 		}
